    {
      "id": "9LfPK",
      "text": "If atomic weight of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math>, respectively, then the empirical formula of compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>.",
